---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../../components/PageIntro.astro';
import CTA from '../../components/CTA.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Bespoke web applications"
  description="Focused web applications built around your people and processes, connected to the business systems you already use."
>
  <PageIntro
    label="Bespoke applications"
    title="Give your workflow a place to work."
    description="Bring the work around your ERP into a focused web application. Built for the people doing the task, with the information they need in reach."
  />
  <section class="section service-area">
    <div class="wrap editorial-split">
      <h2>
        Start with the
        <br />
        missing step.
      </h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Some processes end up spread across spreadsheets, emails and business
          software. People become the connection: copying records, checking
          statuses and passing decisions from one system to another.
        </p>
        <p>
          We build bespoke web applications on OuterForge, our web application
          platform. SAP Service Layer and Produmex API connections, users,
          permissions, email and background jobs are already available. We map
          your process and develop the screens and rules it needs.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/outerforge/">
            See the OuterForge platform <Icon />
          </a>
        </p>
        <p>
          For QC and batch release,{' '}
          <a class="inline-link" href="/solutions/quality-control/">
            OuterForge Quality
          </a>{' '}
          is an existing application on this foundation, ready to configure for
          your specifications and workflow.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section studio-section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2>
          A focused scope.
          <br />
          Room to develop.
        </h2>
        <p>
          Get the useful first workflow working, then build on what you learn.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="service-list">
        <article class="service">
          <h3>Understand the work.</h3>
          <p>
            Walk through the process, exceptions and handoffs with the people
            using it. Agree what a successful first version needs to do.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="service">
          <h3>Build and connect.</h3>
          <p>
            Shape the interface around the task and connect it to the records
            and operations in your existing systems.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article class="service">
          <h3>Put it to work.</h3>
          <p>
            Test the real workflow together. Agree deployment, support and the
            next improvements around practical use.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CTA />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .inline-link {
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: var(--line-strong);
    text-underline-offset: 0.18em;
  }
  .inline-link:hover {
    color: var(--link-hover);
    text-decoration-color: currentColor;
  }
</style>
